WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.440
Think about this: An access gate prohibits
commercial use of individual

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:06.640
lists. What should an agent do?

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:08.380
Let’s work through it together.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:14.400
I'm Doctor Gainz. Lesson 5: Check record-
use and fee restrictions first.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:19.680
Access to government information does not
automatically permit every use of

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:24.200
it. King County’s surplus page expressly
warns against commercial use of

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:28.800
lists of individuals. South Carolina law
restricts knowingly obtaining or

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:32.720
using personal government-record
information for commercial solicitation.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:36.420
These are examples, not a complete
national rule map.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:40.840
Keep a jurisdiction requirements sheet
with the exact official source, the

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:45.100
date reviewed, the activity being
considered, and the unresolved question.

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:50.100
Check access attestations, solicitation,
representation, licensing,

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:53.140
compensation, assignments, and retention.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:57.540
Do not click an acknowledgement that
conflicts with your purpose or use an

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:00.780
agent to cross a gate you could not
truthfully accept yourself.

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:04.340
Fee rules may make a proposed business
model unsuitable.

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:08.460
Jefferson County’s page includes a
waiting-period warning for finder fees.

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:13.080
Read current authority with a qualified
local professional before adopting

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:17.500
any fee structure. A course example from
another state is not permission.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:19.440
Pause and try this.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:22.800
Record two published restrictions from
official sources.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:27.320
Describe how each changes your proposed
activity, without collecting any

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:30.180
claimant information. Quick knowledge
check.

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:34.320
An access gate prohibits commercial use of
individual lists.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:35.980
What should an agent do?

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:39.960
The answer: Stop that use and record the
restriction.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:44.800
Automation must respect the same access
and use restrictions as the person

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:48.740
directing it. Keep the source, the date,
and the unknowns visible.

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:50.360
I'll see you in the next lesson.
